        <a href="/hospitals">Hospitals</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <section class="hero" style="border-top:none;">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">For colleges</span>
      <h1>Your students already drive home.<br />Most of those seats are empty.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Every break, students drive the same corridors with three empty seats while classmates
        pay for a flight or a bus. Seat Sherpa lets them share the drive at cost — and it
        costs your college nothing to run.
      </p>
      <a class="btn" href="mailto:justin@seatsherpa.app?subject=Seat%20Sherpa%20for%20our%20campus&body=Hi%20Justin%2C%0A%0AI%27m%20reaching%20out%20about%20Seat%20Sherpa%20for%20our%20campus.%0A%0ASchool%3A%20%0AMy%20role%3A%20%0ARoughly%20how%20many%20students%20commute%20or%20travel%20home%20for%20breaks%3A%20%0A%0AThanks%2C%0A">Request information →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h2>How it works on campus</h2>
      <p class="sub">No integration, no software to install, and nothing for the college to administer.</p>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step"><div class="n">1</div><div>
          <h3>Students post the drive they're already making</h3>
          <p>Someone heading home to LA for Thanksgiving lists their trip in about a minute, from a browser or the app.</p>
        </div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="n">2</div><div>
          <h3>Classmates find it and book a seat</h3>
          <p>Riders search their route and book online. Payment runs through the platform, so there's no chasing anyone for gas money.</p>
        </div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="n">3</div><div>
          <h3>We can set up a code for your campus</h3>
          <p>A school-specific promo code gives your students a discount on their first ride and lets us report back how many trips it covered.</p>
        </div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="n">4</div><div>
          <h3>Riders who find nothing tell drivers what they need</h3>
          <p>When no ride exists yet, students post the trip they're looking for — and get an email the moment someone posts it.</p>
        </div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Why colleges care</h2>
      <p class="sub">Three problems this touches without a budget line.</p>
      <div class="grid3">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>🅿️ Parking demand</h3>
          <p>Every filled seat is a car that didn't need a space. Nothing to integrate with your parking system — fewer cars is the whole mechanism.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>💸 Cost of getting home</h3>
          <p>Seat prices are capped at the trip's actual driving cost, so a shared ride is structurally cheaper than a flight or a last-minute bus.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>🌱 Sustainability reporting</h3>
          <p>Shared trips on your corridors are measurable. If you use a campus code, we can tell you how many rides and seats it covered.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What it costs</h2>
      <div class="note">
        <strong>Nothing, to the college.</strong> Seat Sherpa is a consumer marketplace — students post and book
        directly, and we take a small service fee on each booked seat. There's no contract, no license, no
        onboarding project, and no IT work. If it doesn't get used on your campus, it costs you nothing.
        <br /><br />
        Seat prices are capped at the trip's shared driving cost (currently up to $55 a seat, or $60 on trips over 400 miles), because this is
        cost-sharing carpooling — not a ride-hail service and not a way for students to run a business.
      </div>
      <!-- Optional paid tier (Justin, 2026-09-06): matches the $2,500 / $3,500
           proposal emailed to 16 campuses on 9/4, so a click-through no longer
           lands on "it costs nothing" alone. -->
      <div class="note" style="margin-top:14px;">
        <strong>Optional: Seat Sherpa Campus.</strong> A branded ride board for your school with .edu verification,
        preset routes for the trips your students actually make, and a term report for your office.
        $2,500 a year for the first three founding campuses, $3,500 after. Students still ride free of any
        institutional fee either way.
        <br /><br />
        <a href="/campus/proposal">See the campus proposal →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container cta">
      <h2 style="margin-bottom:14px;">Want to try it on your campus?</h2>
      <p class="sub" style="margin:0 auto 26px;">
        Tell us your school and the corridors your students travel most. We'll set up a code and a page for
        those routes, and you can see whether it gets traction before committing to anything.
      </p>
      <a class="btn" href="mailto:justin@seatsherpa.app?subject=Seat%20Sherpa%20for%20our%20campus&body=Hi%20Justin%2C%0A%0AI%27m%20reaching%20out%20about%20Seat%20Sherpa%20for%20our%20campus.%0A%0ASchool%3A%20%0AMy%20role%3A%20%0ARoughly%20how%20many%20students%20commute%20or%20travel%20home%20for%20breaks%3A%20%0A%0AThanks%2C%0A">Request information →</a>
      <p style="margin-top:16px;font-size:14px;color:var(--foot);">Or email <a href="mailto:justin@seatsherpa.app">justin@seatsherpa.app</a> directly.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

